# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the runner's tests and e2e runs (zig-test.sh, e2e.sh). Only what
# the network library (runner/rust/zr-net, docs/rust-net.md) makes TSan report falsely belongs here,
# each with why; a report in Zig code that has no Rust frame in either stack is not suppressed.
#
# Zig's ThreadSanitizer instruments Zig code only. The library's tokio workers hand memory to and
# from the Zig threads through Rust's own synchronisation (futexes, atomics, channels), which TSan
# cannot see: the bytes a Zig thread gave the library are read by a worker with no happens-before
# edge in TSan's model, and the other way round, and TSan reports a race at the `memcpy`, `send`,
# `recv` or `free` of the one thread against the other's earlier write. A report matches when any
# frame of either stack is a Rust one (demangled: `tokio::`, `hyper::`, ...). Races inside Rust are
# searched for by Rust's own tools (`cargo test`, and nightly `-Zsanitizer=thread` and loom, in
# docs/rust-net.md, "Validation"), not here.
# Rust frames, demangled, are the only ones whose names have `::` (Zig's have dots): any frame of
# either stack with one matches. This also covers a frame like `<socket2::socket::Socket>::send`.
race:*::*
